@startuml API Components

' ============================================================================
' API Components Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows the internal code structure of the A/B Testing API.
'
' Architecture follows the Repository Pattern:
' - Routers (API endpoints) depend on abstract Repository interfaces
' - dependencies.py provides concrete implementations via dependency injection
' - This allows easy testing and database swapping
'
' Key modules:
' - main.py: FastAPI app entry point, registers routers
' - dependencies.py: Dependency injection, provides Repository instances
' - routers/: API endpoint handlers (/experiments, /events, /flags)
' - repositories/interfaces.py: Abstract contracts + Entity classes
' - repositories/sqlalchemy/: PostgreSQL implementations using SQLAlchemy
' - models.py: SQLAlchemy ORM models
' - schemas.py: Pydantic request/response schemas
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #333333

title A/B Testing API - Component Structure (Repository Pattern)

rectangle "app/" as App #LightBlue {

    rectangle "Entry Point" as Entry #LightGreen {
        [main.py] as Main
        [dependencies.py] as Deps
        note right of Deps
          **Dependency Injection**
          Provides Repository
          instances to Routers
        end note
    }

    rectangle "API Routers" as Routers #LightYellow {
        [experiments.py] as ExpR
        [events.py] as EventR
        [feature_flags.py] as FlagR
    }

    rectangle "Core Services" as Services #LightPink {
        [auth.py] as Auth
        [cache.py] as Cache
    }

    rectangle "repositories/" as RepoDir #Wheat {

        rectangle "Interfaces" as Interfaces #White {
            [interfaces.py] as IRepo
            note right of IRepo
              Entity classes
              Abstract repos
            end note
        }

        rectangle "sqlalchemy/" as SQLADir #LightGray {
            [experiment_repo.py] as ExpImpl
            [event_repo.py] as EventImpl
            [feature_flag_repo.py] as FlagImpl
            note bottom of SQLADir
              **Concrete Implementations**
              SQLAlchemy ORM queries
              Can be swapped for other DBs
            end note
        }
    }

    rectangle "Data Layer" as Data #LightCyan {
        [models.py] as Models
        [schemas.py] as Schemas
        [database.py] as DB
    }

    rectangle "Configuration" as Config #WhiteSmoke {
        [config.py] as Conf
    }
}

database "PostgreSQL" as PG #WhiteSmoke

' Entry point connections
Main --> ExpR
Main --> EventR
Main --> FlagR

' Router dependencies
ExpR --> Auth
EventR --> Auth
FlagR --> Auth

ExpR --> Cache
FlagR --> Cache

' Routers use Repository interfaces (via Deps)
ExpR --> Deps
EventR --> Deps
FlagR --> Deps

Deps --> IRepo : provides
Deps --> ExpImpl
Deps --> EventImpl
Deps --> FlagImpl

' Implementations use Models
ExpImpl --> Models
EventImpl --> Models
FlagImpl --> Models

' Routers use Schemas
ExpR --> Schemas
EventR --> Schemas
FlagR --> Schemas

' Data layer connections
Models --> DB
DB --> PG
DB --> Conf
Auth --> Conf

note right of Routers
  **Endpoints:**
  /experiments/*
  /events/*
  /flags/*

  Depend on interfaces
  not implementations
end note

note bottom of RepoDir
  **Repository Pattern:**
  - interfaces.py: Abstract contracts
  - sqlalchemy/: Concrete implementations
  - Dependency injection via dependencies.py
end note

@enduml
